Helios DXVK fork: any first access of a shared image waits for hand-offs

Conduit guest/windows/docs/shared-surfaces.md section 4. Applied after 0007
by ci/windows/Build-Driver.ps1.

0007 sampled the hand-off ledger only for copy sources and sampled views. A
reader that renders into, clears, UAV-writes or blends onto a shared image
after acquiring it races the producer's pending writes as well. The ledger
is now sampled where every resource access is tracked: the first tracking of
a shared image in a submission (DxvkCommandList::track, once per image and
access kind thanks to trackId) records the hand-off wait, whatever the
usage, and the submission worker waits once per image per submission.

